AB  - To address the dual challenges of inaccurate implicit cultural semantic expression and difficulties in the visual generation of cultural product designs. This study introduces the AI-CPD framework, which utilizes generative artificial intelligence (GAI) tools to enable the symbolic semantic representation of cultural features in cultural product design (CPD). The framework integrates Large Language Models (LLMs), Large Reconstruction Models (LRMs), and Latent Diffusion Models (LDMs) to provide designers with a structured and intelligent design support system. Using the Miao fish culture in China as a case study, this research conducts quantitative comparative experiments with three mainstream large models to validate the design effectiveness of the AI-CPD framework. This framework enhances designers’ ability to express implicit cultural semantics, retrieve cultural information efficiently, and visualize cultural meaning throughout the design process.
