AB  - This chapter introduces advanced generative AI models—focusing on both Diffusion Models and Transformers—that underpin today's cutting-edge systems such as ChatGPT and StableDiffusion. We begin by presenting the fundamental concepts and methodologies behind Diffusion Models, including discrete-time frameworks like DDPM and DDIM, as well as score matching and flow matching techniques. Advanced topics, including diffusion models for text generation and latent diffusion models, are also discussed. The chapter then delves into the principles of Transformers, providing comprehensive guidance on building Large Language Models (LLMs) and applying these models across a variety of NLP tasks. Finally, we examine the current limitations of Transformer-based models and survey emerging research directions aimed at overcoming these challenges and pushing the boundaries of generative AI.
