AB  - The transition towards smart grids, characterized by digitization, renewable integration, and decentralized operations, has rendered power systems increasingly complex and data-intensive. In this context, compliance auditing of power data is crucial for ensuring safe and fair operations but faces significant challenges. Current methods, relying on manual inspection or static rule-based checking, are inefficient, error-prone, and struggle to cope with the volume, variety, and evolving nature of modern grid data. To address these issues, this paper proposes PowerAuditGPT, a novel automated auditing model that leverages large language models (LLMs) enhanced with domain-specific knowledge. The model uniquely integrates a Prompt-Power guidance mechanism and a GAIA intelligent analysis module to accurately identify compliance issues in both market operations and household consumption data. Comprehensive experiments on the PJM Electricity Market and UCI Household Power Consumption datasets demonstrate that PowerAuditGPT significantly outperforms traditional and mainstream machine learning methods across key metrics, including precision, recall, and F1-score. The results validate its high accuracy and efficiency in handling complex power data audits. This work presents a robust intelligent framework for power data compliance auditing, with its demonstrated high accuracy and automation presenting a viable path toward scalable, intelligent compliance monitoring for modern smart grids.
